title: Bundestag Elections
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: (year = next_election_year and month >= next_election_month) or (year > next_election_year)
on-departure: month_actions += 1; in_election = 0; next_election_year = next_election_year + 4; n_elections += 1; next_election_time = time + 48;
set-jump: post_election_1928
face-image: img/Rothe_Wahlen_1903.jpg

# the low priority means that this event is only seen after all other events are resolved for the month.

# The first election is the regular one on 25 March 2029. Regular elections follow every four years
# (March 2033, 2037, 2041, ...). An early election moves the four-year cycle.
#
# The government that forms after each election sets "timeline":
#   1 = the centre holds: CDU/CSU-SPD, Kenya, a tolerated CDU/CSU minority government, or a centre government without the SPD
#   2 = the left turn: red-red-green or an SPD majority
#   3 = the firewall falls: the CDU/CSU governs with the AfD
#
# The coalitions and their flags are listed in apply_government.scene.dry.

= Bundestag election, [+ month : month +] [+ year +]

[? if n_elections = 0 : Sunday, 25 March 2029. After four hard years of the CDU/CSU–SPD coalition, Germany elects the 22nd Bundestag. Growth is weak, prices are high, and the AfD hopes to become the strongest party in the country for the first time. As a governing party, we will be judged on the record of this coalition. ?]

[? if n_elections > 0 and timeline = 1 : Germany votes again. The parties of the centre have carried the republic through another term. The voters will now decide whether holding the centre was enough, or whether they have had their fill of compromise. ?]

[? if n_elections > 0 and timeline = 2 : Germany votes again. For the first time in the history of the Federal Republic, the country has been governed from the left. This election is a referendum on that experiment, and the CDU/CSU and the AfD are both campaigning to end it. ?]

[? if n_elections > 0 and timeline = 3 : Germany votes again. The Brandmauer is gone: the CDU/CSU has governed with the AfD. We have spent this term as the leading voice of the democratic opposition, and this election may be the chance to turn the country around. ?]

The polling stations close at 18:00.

- @election_algorithm: May we do our best...

@post_election_1928
on-arrival: {!
// set old results
// election threshold constitutional reform
// banning parties
var new_party_sum = 0;
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    Q['old_' + party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_r'];
    if (Q.electoral_threshold > 0) {
        // exempt from the threshold: the SSW (national minority) and parties with 3 direct mandates
        var exempt = party == 'ssw' || (Q.direct_mandate_rule && Q[party + '_direct'] >= 3);
        if ((Q[party + '_normalized']*100 < Q.electoral_threshold && !exempt) || (Q.electoral_threshold > 1 && party == 'other') || Q[party + '_banned']) {
            Q[party + '_r'] = 0;
        } else {
            // exact share, so that a small party like the SSW is not rounded away
            Q[party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_normalized']*100;
        }
        new_party_sum += Q[party + '_r'];
    } else {
        Q[party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_votes'];
    }
    // if we use decimals, then we might want to truncate the numbers
    if (Q.use_decimals) {
        Q[party + '_r_disp'] = Q[party+'_r'].toFixed(1);
    }  else {
            Q[party + '_r_disp'] = Q[party+'_r'];
    }
    Q['change_' + party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_r'] - Q['old_' + party + '_r'];
    var sign = Q['change_' + party + '_r'] > 0 ? '+'  : '';
    Q['str_change_' + party] = sign + Q['change_' + party + '_r'];//.toFixed(1);
}
// calculate new party sum if electoral reform
if (Q.electoral_threshold && Q.electoral_threshold > 0) {
    for (var party of Q.parties) {
        if (Q[party + '_r'] > 0) {
            if (Q.use_decimals) {
                Q[party + '_r'] = Math.round(Q[party + '_r']*1000/new_party_sum)/10;
            } else {
                Q[party + '_r'] = Math.round(Q[party + '_r']*100/new_party_sum);
            }
        }
        if (Q.use_decimals) {
            Q[party + '_r_disp'] = Q[party+'_r'].toFixed(1);
        } else {
            Q[party + '_r_disp'] = Q[party+'_r'];
        }
        Q['change_' + party + '_r'] = Math.round((Q[party + '_r'] - Q['old_' + party + '_r'])*10)/10;
        var sign = Q['change_' + party + '_r'] > 0 ? '+'  : '';
        Q['str_change_' + party] = sign + Q['change_' + party + '_r'];//.toFixed(1);
    }
    // rounding can leave the total at 99.9 or 100.1: the largest party takes the difference
    var seat_sum = 0;
    var largest = Q.parties[0];
    for (var party of Q.parties) {
        seat_sum += Q[party + '_r'];
        if (Q[party + '_r'] > Q[largest + '_r']) {
            largest = party;
        }
    }
    Q[largest + '_r'] = Math.round((Q[largest + '_r'] + 100 - seat_sum)*10)/10;
    Q[largest + '_r_disp'] = Q.use_decimals ? Q[largest + '_r'].toFixed(1) : Q[largest + '_r'];
    Q['change_' + largest + '_r'] = Math.round((Q[largest + '_r'] - Q['old_' + largest + '_r'])*10)/10;
    Q['str_change_' + largest] = (Q['change_' + largest + '_r'] > 0 ? '+' : '') + Q['change_' + largest + '_r'];
}

// The largest party. Ties go to the SPD.
Q.largest_party = 'SPD';
var largest_r = Q.spd_r;
if (Q.cdu_r + Q.csu_r > largest_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'CDU/CSU';
    largest_r = Q.cdu_r + Q.csu_r;
}
if (Q.afd_r > largest_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'AfD';
    largest_r = Q.afd_r;
}
if (Q.greens_r > largest_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'Grüne';
    largest_r = Q.greens_r;
}
if (Q.linke_r > largest_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'Linke';
    largest_r = Q.linke_r;
}

// coalitions (% of seats). cdu_r is the whole CDU/CSU unless csu_split = 1.
var union_r = Q.cdu_r + Q.csu_r;
var sapd_r = Q.sapd_r || 0;
var srpd_r = Q.srpd_r || 0;
// Große Koalition: CDU/CSU + SPD
Q.grand_coalition = union_r + Q.spd_r + srpd_r;
// Kenia: CDU/CSU + SPD + Grüne
Q.kenya_coalition = union_r + Q.spd_r + Q.greens_r + srpd_r;
// Deutschland: CDU/CSU + SPD + FDP
Q.germany_coalition = union_r + Q.spd_r + Q.fdp_r + srpd_r;
// Brombeer: CDU/CSU + BSW + SPD
Q.blackberry_coalition = union_r + Q.spd_r + Q.bsw_r + srpd_r;
// Rot-Grün: SPD + Grüne
Q.red_green_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.greens_r;
// Ampel: SPD + Grüne + FDP
Q.traffic_light_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.greens_r + Q.fdp_r;
// Rot-Rot: SPD + Linke
Q.red_red_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.linke_r + sapd_r;
// Rot-Rot-Grün: SPD + Grüne + Linke
Q.left_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.greens_r + Q.linke_r + sapd_r;
// Rot-Lila: SPD + BSW
Q.red_purple_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.bsw_r;
// Rot-Blau: SPD + AfD
Q.red_blue_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.afd_r;
// a centre government without the SPD: CDU/CSU + Grüne + FDP (Schwarz-Grün, Schwarz-Gelb or Jamaika)
Q.black_green_coalition = union_r + Q.greens_r + Q.fdp_r;
// Schwarz-Blau: CDU/CSU + AfD, only possible if the firewall falls
Q.right_coalition = union_r + Q.afd_r;
// all the parties of the democratic centre
Q.neo_weimar_coalition = union_r + Q.spd_r + Q.greens_r + Q.fdp_r + srpd_r;
// Progressive coalition isn't a distinct coalition, but it's the majority that lets you pass social reforms
Q.progressive_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.linke_r + Q.greens_r + Q.ssw_r + sapd_r + srpd_r;

for (var c of ['grand_coalition', 'kenya_coalition', 'germany_coalition', 'blackberry_coalition', 'red_green_coalition', 'traffic_light_coalition', 'red_red_coalition', 'left_coalition', 'red_purple_coalition', 'red_blue_coalition', 'black_green_coalition', 'right_coalition', 'neo_weimar_coalition', 'progressive_coalition']) {
    Q[c] = Math.round(Q[c]*10)/10;
}

Q.grand_coalition_failed = 0;
Q.coalition_dissent = 0;
Q.linke_coalition_dissent = 0;
// Until a government is formed there is none. apply_government sets all the flags and ministers.
Q.coalition = 'none';

// reset the goals of the Linke as a coalition partner
Q.kpd_goals_seen = 0;
Q.kpd_ultimatum_seen = 0;
Q.welfare_goal = 0;
Q.agriculture_goal = 0;
Q.economy_goal = 0;
Q.finance_goal = 0;
Q.labor_goal = 0;
Q.foreign_goal = 0;
Q.interior_goal = 0;
Q.reichswehr_goal = 0;

Q.welfare_goal_completed = 0;
Q.agriculture_goal_completed = 0;
Q.economy_goal_completed = 0;
Q.finance_goal_completed = 0;
Q.labor_goal_completed = 0;
Q.foreign_goal_completed = 0;
Q.interior_goal_completed = 0;
Q.reichswehr_goal_completed = 0;

Q.strike_term_seen = 0;

// understanding the enemy
if (Q.afd_r >= 15) {
    Q.understanding_enemy_timer = 2;
}

var election_result = {'date': new Date(Q.year, Q.month - 1)};
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    election_result[party] = Q[party + '_r'];
}
Q.election_records.push(election_result);
!}
on-departure: afd_urgency = 1 if (afd_urgency == 0 and afd_r >= 15)
on-display: {!
data = [
    {
        "id": "linke",
        "legend": "Linke",
        "name": "Linke",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.linke_r*5),
    }
];
if (Q.sapd_formed && Q.sapd_r) {
    data.push({
            "id": "sapd",
            "legend": "SAPD",
            "name": "SAPD",
            "seats": Math.round(Q.sapd_r*5),
            });
}

data.push({
        "id": "spd",
        "legend": "SPD",
        "name": "SPD",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.spd_r*5),
});

if (Q.srpd_formed && Q.srpd_r) {
    data.push({
            "id": "srpd",
            "legend": "SRPD",
            "name": "SRPD",
            "seats": Math.round(Q.srpd_r*5),
            });
}
data = data.concat([
    {
        "id": "greens",
        "legend": "Grüne",
        "name": "Grüne",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.greens_r*5),
    },
    {
        "id": "ssw",
        "legend": "SSW",
        "name": "SSW",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.ssw_r*5),
    },
    {
        "id": "fdp",
        "legend": "FDP",
        "name": "FDP",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.fdp_r*5),
    },
    {
        "id": "cdu",
        "legend": Q.csu_split ? "CDU" : "CDU/CSU",
        "name": Q.csu_split ? "CDU" : "CDU/CSU",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.cdu_r*5),
    },
    {
        "id": "csu",
        "legend": "CSU",
        "name": "CSU",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.csu_r*5),
    },
    {
        "id": "other",
        "legend": "Other",
        "name": "Other",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.other_r*5),
    },
    {
        "id": "bsw",
        "legend": "BSW",
        "name": "BSW",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.bsw_r*5),
    },
    {
        "id": "afd",
        "legend": "AfD",
        "name": "AfD",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.afd_r*5),
    },
]);

if (window && d3) {
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    }

    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);
}
!}
go-to: firewall_forced if firewall_erosion >= 8 and right_coalition >= 50 and spd_r < 50; coalition_menu if firewall_erosion < 8 or right_coalition < 50 or spd_r >= 50

= Election results

{!<svg id="reichstag" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<table>!}
{!<tr><td>Party</td><td>Seat share</td><td>% Change</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#E3000F; outline: 2px; outline-style: solid;'> </div> !} **SPD:** {!</td><td>!} **[+ spd_r +]%** {!</td><td>!} **[+ str_change_spd +]** {!</td></tr>!}

[? if sapd_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#C40000'> </div> !}SAPD: {!</td><td>!} [+ sapd_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_sapd +] {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if srpd_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#F4A460'> </div> !}SRPD: {!</td><td>!} [+ srpd_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_srpd +] {!</td></tr>!} ?]

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#000'> </div> !} [? if csu_split = 0 : CDU/CSU ?][? if csu_split = 1 : CDU ?]: {!</td><td>!} [+ cdu_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_cdu +] {!</td></tr>!}

[? if csu_split = 1 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#0080C9'> </div> !} CSU: {!</td><td>!} [+ csu_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_csu +] {!</td></tr>!} ?]

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#009EE0'> </div> !} AfD: {!</td><td>!} [+ afd_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_afd +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#46962B'> </div> !} Grüne: {!</td><td>!} [+ greens_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_greens +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#B61C3E'> </div> !} Linke: {!</td><td>!} [+ linke_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_linke +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#C8A800'> </div> !} FDP: {!</td><td>!} [+ fdp_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_fdp +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#542344'> </div> !} BSW: {!</td><td>!} [+ bsw_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_bsw +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#003C8F'> </div> !} SSW: {!</td><td>!} [+ ssw_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_ssw +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#a0a0a0'> </div> !} Others: {!</td><td>!} [+ other_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_other +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}

**Possible majorities:**

[? if grand_coalition >= 50 : Große Koalition (CDU/CSU + SPD): [+ grand_coalition +]% ?]

[? if kenya_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition < 50 : Kenia (CDU/CSU + SPD + Grüne): [+ kenya_coalition +]% ?]

[? if germany_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition < 50 and fdp_r > 0 : Deutschland (CDU/CSU + SPD + FDP): [+ germany_coalition +]% ?]

[? if blackberry_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition < 50 and bsw_r > 0 : Brombeer (CDU/CSU + BSW + SPD): [+ blackberry_coalition +]% ?]

[? if red_green_coalition >= 50 : Rot-Grün (SPD + Grüne): [+ red_green_coalition +]% ?]

[? if traffic_light_coalition >= 50 and red_green_coalition < 50 and fdp_r > 0 : Ampel (SPD + Grüne + FDP): [+ traffic_light_coalition +]% ?]

[? if red_red_coalition >= 50 : Rot-Rot (SPD + Linke): [+ red_red_coalition +]% ?]

[? if left_coalition >= 50 and red_green_coalition < 50 and red_red_coalition < 50 : Rot-Rot-Grün (SPD + Grüne + Linke): [+ left_coalition +]% ?]

[? if red_purple_coalition >= 50 and bsw_r > 0 : Rot-Lila (SPD + BSW): [+ red_purple_coalition +]% ?]

[? if red_blue_coalition >= 50 : Rot-Blau (SPD + AfD): [+ red_blue_coalition +]% ?]

[? if black_green_coalition >= 50 : Without the SPD (CDU/CSU + Grüne + FDP): [+ black_green_coalition +]% ?]

[? if right_coalition >= 50 : Schwarz-Blau (CDU/CSU + AfD): [+ right_coalition +]% ?]

[? if largest_party = "AfD" : For the first time, the AfD is the strongest party in the Bundestag. Its leaders are claiming the chancellorship, and every eye is now on the CDU/CSU. ?]

[? if largest_party = "SPD" : We are the strongest party in the Bundestag. The task of forming a government falls to us. ?]

[? if right_coalition >= 50 and firewall_erosion >= 4 and firewall_erosion < 8 : Voices in the CDU/CSU are openly asking why the party should keep refusing a majority that already exists on the right. The firewall is under strain. ?]

[? if firewall_erosion >= 8 and right_coalition >= 50 and spd_r < 50 : On election night, leading figures of the CDU/CSU announce "talks with all parties that the voters have sent to the Bundestag". Everyone understands what this means. ?]

There are several ways in which a government could be formed.

@coalition_menu

- @spd_majority
- @red_green_coalition
- @red_red_coalition
- @left_coalition
- @traffic_light_coalition
- @grand_coalition
- @kenya_coalition
- @germany_coalition
- @blackberry_coalition
- @red_purple_coalition
- @spd_minority
- @red_blue_coalition
- @no_majority
- @toleration
- @opposition


@spd_majority
title: SPD-Alleinregierung
subtitle: We have won an absolute majority, and will govern alone.
view-if: spd_r >= 50
on-arrival: coalition = "spd_allein"; pro_republic += 5
call: apply_government

We have won an absolute majority in the Bundestag, something that no party has managed since 1957. We can govern alone.

Who should be our chancellor?

- @klingbeil
- @pistorius
- @bas

@spd_minority
title: SPD-Minderheitsregierung
subtitle: Govern alone without a majority, law by law, tolerated by other parties.
unavailable-subtitle: No other parties are willing to tolerate us. This needs decent relations with both the Grüne and the Linke, or very good relations with the CDU/CSU.
view-if: largest_party = "SPD" and spd_r < 50
choose-if: (left_coalition >= 50 and greens_relation >= 30 and linke_relation >= 30) or (grand_coalition >= 50 and cdu_relation >= 60)
on-arrival: coalition = "spd_minority"; pro_republic -= 2
call: apply_government

We will form a minority government. Every law and every budget will need votes from outside the cabinet, and a single failed vote can bring us down. In return, every ministry is ours.

Who should be our chancellor?

- @klingbeil
- @pistorius
- @bas


@klingbeil
title: Lars Klingbeil for Chancellor
subtitle: The party chairman is the obvious choice, and is acceptable to our partners.
on-arrival: chancellor = "Klingbeil"; chancellor_party = "SPD"
go-to: ministries if in_spd_majority = 0 and in_minority_government = 0

Lars Klingbeil will be elected chancellor by the Bundestag.

@pistorius
title: Boris Pistorius for Chancellor
subtitle: Pistorius is the most popular politician in the country, but the left of the party distrusts him.
on-arrival: chancellor = "Pistorius"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; left_dissent += 5; new_middle_spd += 2; pensioners_spd += 2
go-to: ministries if in_spd_majority = 0 and in_minority_government = 0

Boris Pistorius will be elected chancellor by the Bundestag. The public approves; the Parlamentarische Linke is less enthusiastic.

@bas
title: Bärbel Bas for Chancellor
subtitle: Bas is close to the unions and the party left. Our partners will want something in return.
on-arrival: chancellor = "Bas"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; left_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 3; reformist_dissent += 3; leverage -= 5 if in_spd_majority = 0 and in_minority_government = 0
go-to: ministries if in_spd_majority = 0 and in_minority_government = 0

Bärbel Bas will be elected chancellor by the Bundestag. The unions and the party left are pleased.


@red_green_coalition
title: Rot-Grün
subtitle: SPD and Grüne
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the Grüne are too poor.
view-if: red_green_coalition >= 50 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: greens_relation >= 40
on-arrival: coalition = "rot_gruen"; greens_relation += 5
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

Red-green has a majority of its own, for the first time since the Schröder years.

@red_red_coalition
title: Rot-Rot
subtitle: SPD and Linke
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the Linke are not good enough.
view-if: red_red_coalition >= 50 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: linke_relation >= 50
on-arrival: coalition = "rot_rot"; linke_relation += 10; cdu_relation -= 10; firewall_erosion += 2; capital_strike_progress += 1; kpd_goals_seen = 0
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

A coalition of SPD and Linke alone has governed in the eastern states, but never at the federal level. The Linke would have to accept NATO and the commitments to Ukraine in practice. Business associations warn of an investment strike, and the CDU/CSU declares "total opposition".

@left_coalition
title: Rot-Rot-Grün
subtitle: SPD, Grüne and Linke
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the Grüne and the Linke are not good enough.
view-if: left_coalition >= 50 and red_green_coalition < 50 and red_red_coalition < 50 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: linke_relation >= 40 and greens_relation >= 40

Together with the Grüne and the Linke, we would have a majority in the Bundestag. Such a coalition has governed in the states, but never at the federal level. The Linke would have to accept NATO and the commitments to Ukraine in practice, and the CDU/CSU would be pushed into opposition next to the AfD.

- @left_coalition_relations
- @left_coalition_resources
- @coalition_menu: Try a different governing arrangement.

@left_coalition_relations
title: Our good relations with both parties make an agreement possible.
choose-if: linke_relation >= 60 and greens_relation >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: This needs very good relations with both the Linke and the Grüne.
go-to: left_coalition_success

@left_coalition_resources
title: Use our resources to smooth things over.
subtitle: -3 resources
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough resources.
choose-if: resources >= 3
on-arrival: resources -= 3
go-to: left_coalition_success

@left_coalition_success
on-arrival: coalition = "r2g"; linke_relation += 10; greens_relation += 5; cdu_relation -= 10; firewall_erosion += 2; capital_strike_progress += 1; kpd_goals_seen = 0
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

The coalition agreement is signed. For the first time, the Federal Republic will be governed by a coalition of the left. Business associations warn of an investment strike, and the CDU/CSU declares "total opposition". Some of its members now ask aloud whether the firewall to the AfD still makes sense.

@traffic_light_coalition
title: Ampel
subtitle: SPD, Grüne and FDP
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the Grüne and the FDP are not good enough. Nobody has forgotten how the last Ampel ended.
view-if: traffic_light_coalition >= 50 and red_green_coalition < 50 and fdp_r > 0 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: greens_relation >= 40 and fdp_relation >= 40
on-arrival: coalition = "ampel"; fdp_relation += 5; left_dissent += 3
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

A new traffic light. The first one collapsed in November 2024 over the budget, and all three parties paid for it. This time, the FDP insists on the Finance Ministry and the debt brake in writing.

@grand_coalition
title: Große Koalition
subtitle: CDU/CSU and SPD
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the CDU/CSU are too poor.
view-if: grand_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition_failed == 0 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: cdu_relation >= 30
on-arrival: coalition = "groko"
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

[? if n_elections <= 1 : It would be the continuation of the coalition that we have just campaigned through, and many of our members are tired of it. ?]

@kenya_coalition
title: Kenia-Koalition
subtitle: CDU/CSU, SPD and Grüne
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the CDU/CSU and the Grüne are too poor.
view-if: kenya_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition < 50 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: cdu_relation >= 30 and greens_relation >= 40
on-arrival: coalition = "kenya"
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

CDU/CSU and SPD have no majority on their own, so the Grüne are needed as a third partner. Three parties will have to share the cabinet.

@germany_coalition
title: Deutschland-Koalition
subtitle: CDU/CSU, SPD and FDP
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the CDU/CSU and the FDP are too poor.
view-if: germany_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition < 50 and fdp_r > 0 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: cdu_relation >= 30 and fdp_relation >= 35
on-arrival: coalition = "deutschland"; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 3
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

Black, red and gold: CDU/CSU and SPD have no majority on their own, so the FDP is needed as a third partner. With two partners to our right, the party left and the unions fear for our programme.

@blackberry_coalition
title: Brombeer-Koalition
subtitle: CDU/CSU, BSW and SPD
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the CDU/CSU and the BSW are too poor.
view-if: blackberry_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition < 50 and bsw_r > 0 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: cdu_relation >= 30 and bsw_relation >= 40
on-arrival: coalition = "brombeer"; reformist_dissent += 5; west_relation -= 1
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

The "blackberry" model from Thuringia comes to Berlin. The BSW demands a say on Ukraine and on the stationing of American missiles, which worries our Atlanticists and our allies.

@red_purple_coalition
title: Rot-Lila
subtitle: SPD and BSW
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the BSW are not good enough.
view-if: red_purple_coalition >= 50 and bsw_r > 0 and spd_r < 50
choose-if: bsw_relation >= 45
on-arrival: coalition = "rot_lila"; reformist_dissent += 8; greens_relation -= 5; west_relation -= 1
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

The Brandenburg model comes to Berlin: a coalition with Sahra Wagenknecht's party. It is generous on pensions and wages, and deeply awkward on Russia, NATO and migration.

@red_blue_coalition
title: Rot-Blau
subtitle: SPD and AfD. This would break the firewall with our own hands.
view-if: red_blue_coalition >= 50 and spd_r < 50

A coalition of the SPD with the AfD. Nobody in the party leadership has ever said these words aloud. Even raising the idea would be treated as a betrayal of 160 years of party history: the factions would revolt, members would leave in tens of thousands, and every other democratic party would break with us.

- @red_blue_sure: Do it anyway.
- @coalition_menu: No. Try a different governing arrangement.

@red_blue_sure
on-arrival: coalition = "rot_blau"; left_dissent += 40; center_dissent += 30; labor_dissent += 30; reformist_dissent += 20; greens_relation -= 40; linke_relation -= 40; cdu_relation -= 20; afd_relation += 30; pro_republic -= 15; firewall_erosion = 10; afd_urgency = 0; new_middle_spd -= 8; workers_spd -= 3; pensioners_spd -= 4; catholics_spd -= 2
call: apply_government
go-to: coalition_spd_lead if coalition_leader_party = "SPD"; coalition_other_lead if coalition_leader_party != "SPD"

= Rot-Blau

The coalition agreement with the AfD is signed in front of a wall of cameras. Outside the Willy-Brandt-Haus, our own youth organisation is burning its membership cards. The firewall is gone, and it is we who tore it down.

@coalition_other_lead

The [+ coalition_leader_label +] is the stronger partner, and so [+ coalition_leader +] claims the chancellorship.

- @join_junior: Join the government under Chancellor [+ coalition_leader +].
- @toleration
- @opposition
- @coalition_menu: What are the other governing arrangements?

@join_junior
on-arrival: left_dissent += 3
go-to: ministries

We will govern as the junior partner. The party left grumbles.

@coalition_spd_lead

We are the strongest partner, and we are expected to lead the government and name the chancellor.

Who should be the chancellor?

- @klingbeil
- @pistorius
- @bas
- @cdu_chancellor
- @coalition_menu: What are the other governing arrangements?

@cdu_chancellor
title: Let the CDU/CSU have the chancellorship.
subtitle: This is unexpected and will cause internal dissent, but it gives us a better position in negotiating for the cabinet.
view-if: cdu_in_government = 1
on-arrival: left_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; cdu_relation += 10; chancellor = cdu_leader; chancellor_party = "CDU"; leverage += 10
go-to: ministries

This is highly unexpected, and many in our party are criticizing this decision. [+ cdu_leader +] of the CDU will be chancellor.


@no_majority
title: There is no clear governing majority.
view-if: spd_r < 50 and left_coalition < 50 and neo_weimar_coalition < 50
on-arrival: no_majority_elections += 1

None of the usual coalitions has a majority in this Bundestag. Either someone governs with a minority, or the country votes again.

- @toleration
- @opposition
- @new_elections: New elections, then.


@toleration
title: Tolerate a CDU/CSU minority government.
subtitle: We stay out of the cabinet, but keep the government alive and the AfD out.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cdu_relation < 25 : Our relations with the CDU/CSU are too poor. ?][? if neo_weimar_coalition < 50 : Even with our votes, such a government would have no majority. ?]
view-if: spd_r < 50
choose-if: cdu_relation >= 25 and neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: coalition = "cdu_minority"; pro_republic -= 2; left_dissent += 3
call: apply_government

We have decided to tolerate a minority government under Chancellor [+ cdu_leader +]. This means that we will not take part in the cabinet, but that we will vote against any attempt to bring the government down, and negotiate the budget law by law. It keeps the AfD away from power without binding us to the CDU/CSU's programme.


@opposition
title: Go into opposition.
subtitle: Let the others try to form a government. What the CDU/CSU does next is out of our hands.
view-if: spd_r < 50
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 10 if grand_coalition >= 50; center_dissent += 5 if grand_coalition >= 50; left_dissent -= 5
go-to: opposition_centre if black_green_coalition >= 50 and (firewall_erosion < 8 or right_coalition < 50); firewall_falls if right_coalition >= 50 and ((black_green_coalition < 50 and firewall_erosion >= 4) or firewall_erosion >= 8); opposition_no_majority if black_green_coalition < 50 and (right_coalition < 50 or firewall_erosion < 4)

We announce that the SPD will renew itself in opposition.

@opposition_centre
on-arrival: coalition = "jamaika"; coalition = "schwarz_gruen" if cdu_r + csu_r + greens_r >= 50; coalition = "schwarz_gelb" if cdu_r + csu_r + fdp_r >= 50 and fdp_r > 0
call: apply_government

The CDU/CSU forms a government without us: [+ coalition_name +], under Chancellor [+ chancellor +]. The centre holds. We lead the opposition from the left, next to an AfD that leads it from the right.

@opposition_no_majority
on-arrival: no_majority_elections += 1; coalition = "none"
call: apply_government

Without us, there is no majority in the centre, and the CDU/CSU still refuses to govern with the AfD. The firewall holds, for now, but the country has no government.

- @toleration
- @grand_coalition: We will talk to the CDU/CSU after all.
- @new_elections: New elections, then.


@firewall_forced

The CDU/CSU has opened talks with the AfD. After years of erosion, the Brandmauer no longer holds the party together: its eastern state associations and much of its base want a "bürgerliche Mehrheit", and the leadership has stopped resisting.

- @save_firewall
- @firewall_falls: There is nothing we can do.

@save_firewall
title: Offer the CDU/CSU a coalition on their terms, to keep the AfD out of government.
subtitle: We will have very little leverage in the cabinet negotiations, and the party left will be furious.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if grand_coalition < 50 : CDU/CSU and SPD do not have a majority. ?][? if cdu_relation < 50 : Our relations with the CDU/CSU are too poor for them to listen. ?]
choose-if: grand_coalition >= 50 and cdu_relation >= 50
on-arrival: coalition = "groko"; firewall_concession = 1; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; firewall_erosion -= 2
call: apply_government
go-to: join_junior

The moderates in the CDU/CSU take our offer and win the argument inside their party, narrowly. The firewall is saved for another term. The price is ours to pay.

@firewall_falls
on-arrival: coalition = "schwarz_blau"; firewall_erosion = 10; pro_republic -= 10; afd_urgency = 5 if afd_urgency < 5; cdu_relation -= 20; greens_relation += 10; linke_relation += 10; new_middle_spd += 4; workers_spd += 2; pensioners_spd += 2; left_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5
call: apply_government
go-to: firewall_afd_chancellor if chancellor_party = "AfD"; firewall_cdu_chancellor if chancellor_party != "AfD"

= The firewall falls

@firewall_cdu_chancellor

The Brandmauer has fallen. The CDU/CSU and the AfD sign a coalition agreement, and [+ chancellor +] is elected chancellor with the votes of the far right. The AfD takes the Interior Ministry, and with it the Verfassungsschutz that has been watching the party for years.

Hundreds of thousands demonstrate in Berlin, Hamburg, Munich and Leipzig. The unions, the churches and the Grüne and Linke look to us to lead the democratic opposition. We have four years to prepare for the next election.

@firewall_afd_chancellor

The Brandmauer has fallen. As the stronger party, the AfD claims the chancellorship, and the CDU/CSU accepts the role of junior partner. Alice Weidel is elected chancellor of the Federal Republic of Germany.

Hundreds of thousands demonstrate in Berlin, Hamburg, Munich and Leipzig. The unions, the churches and the Grüne and Linke look to us to lead the democratic opposition. We have four years to prepare for the next election, if it is a fair one.


@new_elections
call: apply_government
on-arrival: {!
Q.coalition = 'none';
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 3;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 3;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}
Q.in_election = 1;
Q.pro_republic -= 5;
Q.workers_spd -= 3;
Q.new_middle_spd -= 3;
Q.old_middle_spd -= 3;
Q.rural_spd -= 3;
Q.catholics_spd -= 2;
Q.pensioners_spd -= 2;
Q.workers_afd += 3;
Q.old_middle_afd += 3;
Q.new_middle_afd += 3;
Q.rural_afd += 3;
Q.unemployed_afd += 3;
Q.catholics_afd += 3;
if (Q.pro_republic < 40) {
    Q.cdu_relation -= 5;
    Q.workers_afd += 4;
    Q.old_middle_afd += 4;
    Q.new_middle_afd += 4;
    Q.rural_afd += 4;
    Q.unemployed_afd += 4;
    Q.catholics_afd += 4;
}
if (Q.right_coalition >= 50) {
    Q.firewall_erosion += 1;
}
!}

No government can be formed. After the chancellor election fails in the Bundestag, the Federal President dissolves parliament. The next election is set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +]; until then, the old government stays on in a caretaker role.

The people's faith in the parties of the centre is shaken by this ordeal. The AfD is using the deadlock to claim that the "old parties" can no longer govern the country.


@ministries

We can claim any number of ministries, as far as our leverage goes. Controlling a ministry allows us to directly shape policy in that area. Any ministry that we do not take stays with our partners.

- #mins_1928
- #drop_mins_1928

@labor
title: Labour and Social Affairs
subtitle: Taking the Labour Ministry is expected of us. It holds the largest budget of the federal government.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: labor_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Bas"; labor_minister = "Schweitzer" if chancellor = "Bas"
go-to: ministries

[+ labor_minister +] of the SPD has been appointed Minister of Labour and Social Affairs.

@interior
title: Interior Ministry
subtitle: The Interior Ministry controls the Federal Police and the Verfassungsschutz.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10
view-if: interior_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister = "Faeser"
go-to: ministries

Nancy Faeser of the SPD has been appointed Interior Minister.

@finance
title: Finance Ministry
subtitle: The Finance Ministry controls the federal budget and taxes.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10
view-if: finance_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Klingbeil"; finance_minister = "Kukies" if chancellor = "Klingbeil"
go-to: ministries

[+ finance_minister +] of the SPD has been appointed Finance Minister.

@economic
title: Economy and Energy
subtitle: The Economy Ministry controls broader economic, industrial and energy policy.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10
view-if: economic_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Rehlinger"
go-to: ministries

Anke Rehlinger of the SPD has been appointed Economy Minister.

@justice
title: Justice Ministry
subtitle: The Justice Ministry drafts the laws on courts, civil rights and consumer protection.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: justice_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Hubig"
go-to: ministries

Stefanie Hubig of the SPD has been appointed Justice Minister.

@foreign
title: Foreign Office
subtitle: The Foreign Office usually goes to the second-largest partner in a coalition.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10
view-if: foreign_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Schmid"
go-to: ministries

Nils Schmid of the SPD has been appointed Foreign Minister.


@agriculture
title: Agriculture Ministry
subtitle: This is not our usual domain.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: agriculture_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister = "Backhaus"
go-to: ministries
tags: mins_1928

Till Backhaus of the SPD has been appointed Agriculture Minister.

@reichswehr
title: Defence Ministry
subtitle: The Defence Ministry commands the Bundeswehr in peacetime and controls the rearmament budget.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10
view-if: reichswehr_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Pistorius"; reichswehr_minister = "Möller" if chancellor = "Pistorius"
go-to: ministries

[+ reichswehr_minister +] of the SPD has been appointed Defence Minister.



@no_more
title: No more ministries.
subtitle: [? if leverage >= 10 : We still have some more leverage to gain ministries. ?][? if leverage < 10 : We do not have much leverage left. ?]
tags: mins_1928

This coalition arrangement is tolerable to all.

@drop_labor
title: Drop the Labour Ministry.
view-if: labor_minister_party = "SPD"
on-arrival: labor_minister_party = default_labor_party; labor_minister = default_labor_minister; leverage += 5
tags: drop_mins_1928
go-to: ministries

@drop_interior
title: Drop the Interior Ministry.
view-if: interior_minister_party = "SPD"
on-arrival: interior_minister_party = default_interior_party; interior_minister = default_interior_minister; leverage += 10
tags: drop_mins_1928
go-to: ministries

@drop_finance
title: Drop the Finance Ministry.
view-if: finance_minister_party = "SPD"
on-arrival: finance_minister_party = default_finance_party; finance_minister = default_finance_minister; leverage += 10
tags: drop_mins_1928
go-to: ministries

@drop_economic
title: Drop the Economy Ministry.
view-if: economic_minister_party = "SPD"
on-arrival: economic_minister_party = default_economic_party; economic_minister = default_economic_minister; leverage += 10
